    "body":  "## Exact-head final acceptance — `78c626280629e42567746fecae4363809cfb158b`\n\n- **PASS:** [PR Verify](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283249), [IDE Host](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283129), [Theia Browser Host](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283250), [Theia Browser-Only](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283202), [Pages build/Chromium baseline](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283066), and [real v1.1.0 Interface release ZIP](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45371283102).\n- **Real Chromium-specific markers, Browser-Only:** `STUDIO_INTERFACE_SCHEMA_NATIVE_READONLY_CHROMIUM_PASS` (native languageId `json`, virtual read-only source, left Source column); `STUDIO_BROWSER_LOCAL_INTERFACE_ZIP_PICKER_CHROMIUM_PASS` (input, nonce CSP, cancel); `STUDIO_BROWSER_DEVICE_INTERFACE_ZIP_UPLOAD_CHROMIUM_PASS` (actual CDP file-input selection of a **synthetic** released-shaped ZIP → Webview chunks → extension host → SHA-256/manifest validation). No project-lock mutation in the synthetic browser probe; separate command-level test covers positive explicit lock/reload and tamper rejection.\n- **Browser-pinned GitHub Release:** `STUDIO_INTERFACE_RELEASE_BROWSER_CORS_PROBE` returned `BLOCKED: Failed to fetch` in CI Chromium; the program does not bypass or downgrade the SHA pin. **Use local device ZIP**; exact deployed Pages-origin network behavior remains `NOT_CHECKED`.\n- Main `e716ad1bdb` AI Chat sidebar changes preserved via two-parent merge; mergeable PR, 0 review threads. Editor-only scope; **Compiler v2.1.0 NOT_LINKED** (tracked by #269); no Owner/Runtime authorization or real 5GC production qualification.\n\n## Integration status\n\n- Feature branch rebased by a real two-parent merge commit `3642fb5766` against the latest main `e716ad1bdb` (preserves AI Chat sidebar + all #267 browser tests); subsequent code adds device-upload Chromium acceptance. PR is mergeable, still Draft.\n- [Exact-head Actions](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions): real released ZIP, PR Verify, IDE Host, Browser Host, Browser-Only and Pages. **Do not count a previous SHA as final acceptance.**\n\nImplements the **editor-first scope of #261**: safe immutable Interface Package import, read-only Schema browsing and **Schema-driven CA-SL auto-completion**. Compiler v2.1 integration is explicitly split to #269; this PR does not claim Compiler LINKED/BUILT or Runtime/Owner authorization.\n\n## What this actually adds\n- Import standalone `connectionagent.io/interface-package/v1alpha1` ZIP from the **browser device File API picker** (bounded chunked Webview upload, no network required), or a native workspace file picker where webview support is absent, or an exact GitHub Release owner/repo + tag + asset + **SHA-256** (fail closed on CORS/network, no `latest` fallback). Default release `ca-client-tools v1.1.0` has its exact published digest prefilled.\n- Bounded ZIP decode, CRC, central/local name verification, path/case collision/symlink/zip-bomb checks. Parse root manifest, verify exact file digests, export/Schema ID closure; never rewrite Provider YAML source or published JSON bytes. Write explicitly confirmed, immutable project-local snapshots; detect tamper and suppress stale exports.\n- **Package Explorer:** read-only Tools, Capabilities, Schemas, Evidence and Manifest using native left source group, JSON/YAML native language IDs, shared right-side Schema Preview, sibling `$ref` Definition, version/provenance and **Compiler NOT_LINKED** label.\n- **Same existing CA-SL Language Server**, current Package generation: exact locked ToolCatalog query/input Schema → required-first argument key/type/description and enum/const values; no duplicates before or after caret. `context.request.*` from the local Contract Request YAML Schema; `node.operation.output.*` / `node.observation.output.*` from exported published output Schema only with dominating source DAG/Wait routes. Progressive `context.` and prior-Node path suggestions. Composed/unknown/ambiguous Schemas fail closed. Existing Wait/Predicate/Node completions and Problems remain owned by existing LSP/Audit.\n- Hints are explicitly **AUTH_NOT_CHECKED**. No fabricated Context, Schema, Owner grants, Scope, Compiler artifact or Runtime admission.\n\n## Tests / evidence\n- `npm test`: ZIP safety \u0026 negative inputs; exact release fetch and SHA negative tests; command-level **Add Dependency → pick ZIP → confirm → lock/reload → Package Explorer → native readonly Schema open/Preview → tamper fail closed** with mocked VS Code host, plus source-only argument/context/producer path positive/negative cases.\n- Separate GitHub Actions **real v1.1.0 release asset** test verifies exact published SHA, ZIP/manifest exports and actual callable input/output path completions (`supi`, `pduSessionId`, `status`).\n- Theia Browser-Only/Browser Host real Chromium acceptance exercises **native LSP** request Schema nested/root suggestions and regression of `await-event.wait.output`, native source group/preview and workbench baseline.\n- Exact-head PR Verify, IDE Host, Theia Browser Host, Browser-Only and Pages checks are required. The latter is a PR build/Chromium gate, not an actual production deploy.\n\n## Explicit follow-ups / limitations\n- **#269** owns Compiler v2.1.0 `resolvedDependencies` with independently sourced trusted Owner bindings. A locked ZIP is not authorization and cannot be converted into `trustedBuildContext.dependencyBindings` by inference.\n- The **browser-local ZIP picker** now has a real Chromium File API upload acceptance (synthetic release-shaped file from the device picker → chunked Webview transfer → formal ZIP/manifest verification) plus cancel/security tests; latest exact-head CI is pending. Mocked host import also verifies the explicit lock and tamper denial. The exact GitHub Release URL returned **BLOCKED: Failed to fetch** from CI Chrome (CORS/network) even though independent published asset validation passes; no workaround may bypass the SHA or switch to mutable URL. On such a block, use browser-local ZIP selection. The production Pages origin\u0027s CORS behavior remains **NOT_CHECKED**.\n- Schema-aware Hover/Definition across authored Procedure → imported callable/export, and full externally sourced `context.*` fields beyond the Contract-owned request, are future #261 work.\n\nNo legacy compatibility parser, custom highlighter, extra editor column or new Language Server. **Scope for merge is editor-only** with clear NOT_LINKED UI, not closing #261.",
